From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 15:51:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] thunderbolt: qcom: Add the Glymur USB4 line-interrupt host
 interface

The host interface (NHI) of the Glymur USB4 host router is not a PCI
device and has no MSI-X. All ring interrupts arrive on one wired
interrupt, with a pending, acknowledge, mask and enable register bank
that covers every path, and clear-on-read must be turned off before the
pending causes can be captured.

Add the register access for that bank and an adapter that implements
the interrupt callbacks of struct tb_nhi_ops on it. The adapter
requests the one interrupt with IRQF_NO_SUSPEND, as the control rings
need, gives each ring a message ID, captures and acknowledges the whole
pending bank in the handler and passes each owned cause to
nhi_handle_interrupt(). It can be shut down and prepared again, so the
router can be stopped and restarted while the driver stays bound.

The register layout matches what the platform's Windows driver programs
on the Surface Laptop 8.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
